diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
index 4b4616b10..e5b1fdfaa 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
@@ -11,3 +11,5 @@
 **P-725. `telemetry` re-exports the OpenTelemetry crates of its API.** Under `otel`: `pub use {opentelemetry, opentelemetry_sdk, tracing_opentelemetry, tracing_subscriber}`. `TracerConfig::provider`, the return types of `setup_tracer`, `setup_meter`, `get_tracer`, `get_meter` and `tracing_layer` and the `SpanProcessor` trait `BaggageSpanProcessor` implements come from these 0.x crates, so an application names them through `strands::telemetry::..` and always gets the versions `strands` resolved, as `mcp` and the provider modules do for theirs. Review finding api-4.
 
 **P-726. The telemetry config builders are nameable, and `Exporters` has one.** `telemetry` re-exports `TracerConfigBuilder`, `MeterConfigBuilder`, `ExportersBuilder` and their state modules `tracer_config_builder`, `meter_config_builder`, `exporters_builder` (`state_mod(vis = "pub")`), so a downstream helper can take and return a builder, as with `AgentBuilder`/`agent_builder`. `Exporters` derives `bon::Builder` with `#[builder(default)]` fields (decision #65: public fields, `Default` and a builder): `Exporters::builder().otlp(true).build()`. Review finding api-6.
+
+**P-727. Correction to P-495: `ExtractorContext::tracer` being crate-internal is the plain mapping, not a divergence.** TS marks `ExtractorContext.tracer` `@internal` (`memory/extraction/types.ts:61-64`), so `pub(crate) tracer` maps it directly; the staged `DIVERGENCES.md` replacement for the `Memory spans` row drops the tracer half and keeps only the missing `memory.extractor` attribute (P-494). A `Logging` row is staged as well: TS `configureLogging`/`Logger` have no Rust counterpart because the crate logs through `tracing`. Review finding api-9.
diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
index 29cecd3bd..4c4ba4866 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
@@ -14,3 +14,5 @@
 | api-4 | Fixed: `telemetry` re-exports `opentelemetry`, `opentelemetry_sdk`, `tracing_opentelemetry` and `tracing_subscriber` under `otel` (P-725); test `tests/api_surface.rs::otel::the_opentelemetry_crates_of_the_api_are_re_exported` (lands with the api-6 commit, which adds the `otel` test module) | this commit |
 | api-6 | Fixed: the three builders and their state modules are public and re-exported from `telemetry`; `Exporters` derives `bon::Builder` (P-726); test `tests/api_surface.rs::otel::a_helper_can_take_and_return_the_telemetry_config_builders` (does not compile without the fix) | this commit |
 | api-7 | Fixed: the `setup_tracer` rustdoc states the subscriber ordering rule; compile-checked doc examples on `setup_tracer`, `setup_meter`, `tracing_layer`, `get_tracer`, `get_meter` and `AgentConfig::trace_attributes`; the two TS module examples (OTLP setup, own provider) are in the `telemetry` module doc, guarded for builds without `otel`. The `lib.rs` module-table row already names the OpenTelemetry setup at this tip, so it is unchanged. `cargo test --doc` passes for the eight new examples | this commit |
+| api-9 | Fixed: (a) the "not in this tree yet" notes in `tests/live_telemetry.rs` and `docs/reviews/live.md` are rewritten, and a replacement `PARITY.md` row for `strands-ts/test/integ/telemetry.test.node.ts` is staged; (b) staged `DIVERGENCES.md` replacement of the `Memory spans` row without the tracer half, and P-727 corrects P-495; (c) staged `DIVERGENCES.md` `Logging` row. The module doc of `telemetry` now says the crate logs through `tracing` (api-7 commit) | this commit |
+| api-11 | For the lead (p10fixa owns `telemetry/tracer/memory.rs`): move the two `otel`-only bodies of `current_span_context` and `link_parent` into the `otel_span` module pair of `tracer.rs` (`current_context`, `add_link`) with no-op twins, or import at the top under `#[cfg(feature = "otel")]`. No `pub` item is involved, so there is no signature edit for this track | not changed |
diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/divergences.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/divergences.md
index 5676bd331..78d8c2dcf 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/divergences.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/divergences.md
@@ -1,3 +1,11 @@
 Replaces the row `Extra span attributes`:
 
 | Spans exported besides the agent's | Only spans started through the OpenTelemetry tracer; `logger` calls never reach a span | `tracing` spans at `INFO` and above that the application opens are exported too (they parent under the agent's); with an application-built subscriber, `tracing_layer` exports whatever that subscriber lets through, log lines as span events included, unless the application filters the layer. The layer adds no attributes of its own | `tracing` is the span API of the Rust crate; `setup_tracer` filters its own subscriber to spans at `INFO` and above (P-721) |
+
+Replaces the row `Memory spans`:
+
+| Memory spans | `memory.extract` records `memory.extractor` (the extractor's class name) | No `memory.extractor` attribute | A trait object has no class name (P-494) |
+
+New row:
+
+| Logging | `configureLogging(logger)` and the `Logger` interface, exported from the package root; the default logger prints warnings and errors to the console | No `configure_logging` and no `Logger`: the crate logs through `tracing` events, each with one `message` field in the TS text format, and prints nothing until the application installs a subscriber. The subscriber `setup_tracer` installs exports spans only, so it prints no log lines either | `tracing` is the logging facade of Rust libraries; a second logger hook would duplicate it |
